diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8347b4a..30b6afc 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,23 @@
 # deploy-demo
 
-Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main`.
+Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main` and on every pushed version tag matching `v*`.
+It can also be started manually with `workflow_dispatch`.
 
-This repository is public.
+This repository is public, so the workflow runs on GitHub-hosted runners only.
+
+## AWS authentication
+
+The workflow assumes `arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/deploy-widget` in `eu-north-1` through
+GitHub OIDC. No AWS access keys are stored; delete the `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and
+`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` repository secrets.
+
+The role's trust policy must trust `token.actions.githubusercontent.com` with audience
+`sts.amazonaws.com`, and match the `sub` claim exactly. Tag deployments use a different `sub`
+than branch deployments, so list both, with no wildcard on the repository:
+
+- `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/heads/main`
+- `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/tags/v*` (use `StringLike` for this one only)
+
+## Slack notification
+
+The final step posts to the webhook in the `SLACK_WEBHOOK` secret.
